Usage: glitch [OPTIONS] PATH [OUTPUT]

  PATH is the file or folder to analyze. OUTPUT is an optional file to which
  we can redirect the smells output.

Options:
  --tech [ansible|chef|puppet]    The IaC technology in which the scripts
                                  analyzed are written in.  [required]
  --tableformat [prettytable|latex]
                                  The presentation format of the tables that
                                  show stats about the run.
  --type [script|tasks|vars|block|unknown]
                                  The type of scripts being analyzed.
  --config PATH                   The path for a config file. Otherwise the
                                  default config will be used.
  --module                        Use this flag if the folder you are going to
                                  analyze is a module (e.g. Chef cookbook).
  --dataset                       Use this flag if the folder being analyzed
                                  is a dataset. A dataset is a folder with
                                  subfolders to be analyzed.
  --linter                        This flag changes the output to be more
                                  usable for other interfaces, such as,
                                  extensions for code editors.
  --includeall TEXT               Some files are ignored when analyzing a
                                  folder. For instance, sometimes only
                                  somefolders in the folder structure are
                                  considered. Use this option ifyou want to
                                  analyze all the files with a certain
                                  extension inside a folder. (e.g.
                                  --includeall yml)This flag is only relevant
                                  if you are using the dataset flag.
  --csv                           Use this flag if you want the output to be
                                  in CSV format.
  --smells [design|security]      The type of smells being analyzed.
  --help                          Show this message and exit.
